{"title":"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The surface area of a cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/517a735a01865af5af9c009f3fb3dc923cea7320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 \\text { cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. The volume of this cube is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a0bfa807da3297e36ef19f1c63c65a60b8ea6c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 4 \\text { cm}^{3} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 24 \\text { cm}^{3} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 8 \\text { cm}^{3} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 27 \\text { cm}^{3} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 64 \\text { cm}^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"586\" height=\"21\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the edge length of the cube and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the volume of the cube. Using the surface area, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d276c4fc9987937313848ecac27bdead4d6642a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6l^2 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/0172676d8595f47b654bd8e1ebe95562d655469c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> must be positive because it represents a cube's edge length, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d625d69974ed356b86ba463549f7163f4b5d9a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l = 2 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/52074d9a6b5df071bf1a5e9ef763c3b21673553b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = l^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d625d69974ed356b86ba463549f7163f4b5d9a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l = 2 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b7d06869c175ad995eed699992abb763c03ffcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = 2^3 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 8 \\text { cm}^{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"171\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/P